cinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab is a 2 x 2 x 1cm specimen of fibroadipose tissue incised and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm gritty  stellate nodule  abutting the margin  A thin slice of the specimen is placed in medium for cycle studies and the remainder is entirely submitted in A F  Gross Description by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SMALL NODULE SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Grossly_positive.
