ults with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 32     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1 8cm breast fragment with a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  ill defined  tan mass containing a focal area of hemorrhage and punctate bright yellow color  The tumor extends within 0 2cm of the superficial and deep margins  and 0 4cm of the superior margin  The surrounding breast tissue on the medial and lateral aspects of the mass are firm and white  with minute cysts  The mass including margins are in cassettes A through E  anterior surface overinked blue  and closest superior margin overinked green   with sections of surrounding firm  white breast tissue in cassettes F and G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in five parts  Labeled  add deep margin  left breast  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of cauterized firm  fibrofatty tissue with a blue dye color  sectioned entirely in H through J  Labeled  add superficial margin  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of focally hard  firm  fibrofatty tissue  sectioned and in K and L  Labeled  left breast  add superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fragment of focally firm fibrofatty tissue  sectioned entirely in M through O  Labeled  left sentinel node  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fatty fragment with nodal tissue  The nodal portion is bivalved and submitted entirely in P and Q  Labeled  left axillary content  is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 2cm aggregate of fatty tissue with multiple unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 1 7cm  in cassettes R through U  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SUPERFICIAL AND DEEP MARGINS  AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SUPERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN    EX PART E  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCI