Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 94 at 10 48 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  INVASIVE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  15   SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  WITH PAGETOID SPREAD ALONG THE DUCTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 1cm in greatest diameter  No vascular invasion is seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  The invasive carcinoma and the intraductal component extend to less than 0 1cm from the inked margin in separate sites  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  16 AUG 94 at 16 23                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 AUG 94 at 07 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm breast tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm  ill defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nodule that is about 0 5cm from the inked margin  Representative section frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A F with the nodule in A and B  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Grossly_close_(multifocal/_broad_front).
