Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 49 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INTRADUCTAL  COMEDO  AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED NEAR BIOPSY CAVITY WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION THROUGHOUT THE BREAST AND METASTATIC TO SEVEN OF TWELVE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Multiple microscopic foci of infiltrating ductal carcinoma are present in sections of breast taken away from the biopsy cavity  The resection margins are negative for carcinoma  however carcinoma is present near the deep resection margin  2  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH HEMORRHAGE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HEMOSIDERIN LADEN MACROPHAGES  AND FOAMY HISTIOCYTES  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 40                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring 30 x 20 x 5cm with an attached 13 x 8 x REMOVED_DATE axillary tail  An overlying 22 x 15cm ellipse of skin contains a slightly off center 4 5cm areola with a central grossly unremarkable 8mm nipple  In the upper quadrant in between the outer and inner quadrants is a well healed 4cm scar  3cm deep to this scar is a 3cm biopsy cavity filled with cloudy red fluid and lined by friable tan red tissue  The biopsy cavity is present 3cm from the deep margin  13cm from the inferior margin  5 5cm from the superior margin  13cm from the lateral margin  and 30cm from the axillary tail margin  Sectioning the remainder of the breast reveals grossly unremarkable mature adipose tissue with admixed fibrous bands  SECTION