Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10 38 CLINICAL DATA  Extensive DCIS with invasion  positive margins on lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN IN ONE FOCUS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL LOWER OUTER QUADRANT   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 18 34                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left mastectomy   specimen consists of a mastectomy and has been oriented by the surgeon  The specimen weighs 220 grams and measures 17 0cm x 12 0cm x 3 0cm  There is an ellipse of skin associated with the tissue which measures 4 0cm x 3 0cm  The skin is tan pink and smooth with no dimpling  retraction  or erythema  The areola measures 3 0cm x 1 8cm  The nipple measures 1 0cm x 0 8cm x 0 5cm  The nipple is grossly normal  The anterior margin is inked blue the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a dense fibrous sub areolar region measuring 3 0cm x 2 0cm x 2 0cm  No additional lesions or masses are identified  The biopsy cavity and surrounding fibrous tissue are sampled in blocks A L  The specimen was received labelled with the patient s name and unit number and is designated as  additional tissue  lower outer quadrant   The specimen consists of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is not oriented by the surgeon  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal firm gray white fibrofatty tissue  No focal lesions are identified  The specimen was entirely submitted in blocks M Q  Resident  GREGORY D  SEIDEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Mary Catherine Hertl  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST LEFT ADDITIONAL LOWER OUTER QUADRANT  EXCIS , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  Excision right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN AND FOCALLY LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU LIMITED TO THE REGION OF THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is present  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL CAVITY    REEXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    REEXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 6 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Tumor focally extends beyond the lymph node capsule in one lymph node  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 03 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four specimens  Labeled  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 2 3cm specimen of fatty breast tissue with a short and a long stitch for orientation  The long stitch is designated lateral and the short superior  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm firm  circumscribed  whitish lesion with a 3mm margin of fat anteriorly  but abutting the posterior surface  covered only by a thin membrane  All other margins are widely free of tumor  Samples of tumor taken for the tissue bank and frozen for Cox 5  The red and green ink designates the anterior  blue and yellow the posterior aspect of the specimen  Representative sections of the tumor in relationship to the closest margins in A through D  Representative sections of normal appearing fatty breast parenchyma from the lateral and medial extremes of the specimens in E and F  Labeled  re excision medial half of biopsy cavity  including deep new margin  short superior  long new medial   is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm oriented fibrofatty specimen  The posterior aspect is inked in black  The inner wall of the biopsy cavity is inked red  and the medial anterior aspects in green  Representative sections submitted in G J  Labeled  final shaved margin   is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring 4 x 4 x 1cm  Representative sections submitted in K N  Labeled  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 3cm fibrofatty tissue specimen  lymph nodes dissected out and submitted in O R  Resident  Frank P  Fechner  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  CLOSE TO POSTERIOR MARGIN  ALL OTHER MARGINS FREE  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL CAVITY    RE EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    RE EXCISION   report_end  , Negative.
