 stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 49     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  are five fragments of fibroadipose breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in aggregate  The largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal multiple firm nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A D  The second largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and is sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast parenchyma  Representative sections of which are submitted in cassettes E H  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm nodular fragment is fibroadipose tissue with pink tan parenchyma is also present half of the specimen is submitted in cassette I  The remaining two fragments consists predominantly of unremarkable soft yellow fat and measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm in aggregate  Representative sections are submitted in cassette J  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  