Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 29 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcioma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 19 32                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 6cm left mastectomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm portion of skin  A stitch marks the 12 o clock orientation  The skin has a 7 3cm linear scar  The surgical resection margin is black inked  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm cavity that lies 2 1cm from the deep margin and 5 2cm from the epidermis  The breast parenchyma away from the cavity is tan yellow  smooth and lobulated with focal tan white fibrotic areas around the cavity  No nodules or masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section code  A B  cavity wall closest to deep resection margin  C D  deep resection margin closest to cavity wall  E F  representative sections of cyst wall  G H  breast parenchyma away from the lesion  G is from fibrotic area adjacent to the cyst   The lateral edge of specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty lobulated parenchyma without grossly identifiable lymph nodes  Resident  ANDRAS SCHAFFER  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE M