Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 27 CLINICAL DATA  37 year old healthy woman with no family history of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  TWO SMALL FOCI  SEE TABLE 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH NUMEROUS SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMAS  PAPILLOMATOSIS  AND FOCAL ATYPIA  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Two microscopic foci on 2 of 8 blocks  D G   the larger focus spanning up to 0 2cm  Grade  2  necrosis  intermediate nuclear grade  Calcifications  Limited to benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to within 0 2cm of a margin of the specimen in one focus  D   Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 22 01 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is an excisional biopsy of fibroadipose breast tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  The surgical margin is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal nodular areas of whitish yellow discoloration and small cyst measuring about 0 1cm in diameter  There is another small fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue in the same container which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and cut section shows areas of whitish yellow discoloration and also small cyst  This specimen is submitted entirely as follows  A G  The larger mass  H  The smaller nodule  Resident  BIZHAN BANDARCHI CHAMKHALEH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT