 0 1cm from the portion of skeletal muscle  Between the muscle and the skin ellipse  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue adjacent to the cavity which is firm  pale yellow and lobulated  There is no gross evidence of infiltrating carcinoma  Section Code  A B  firm area  C E  cavity wall  F  surrounding tissue  G  skin  Labeled  Left axillary node dissection  is a 9 x 5 x 1cm portion of adipose tissue containing lymph nodes up to 1 2cm in size  Many of the nodes grossly are replaced by tumor  and in these areas the nodes cannot be separated from the surrounding adipose tissue  The largest node shows fatty replacement  Sections from each of the nodes are submitted as H   M  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION  LEFT  PART B  RE EXCISION FOR CA PARTIAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Grossly_positive.
