Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 35 CLINICAL DATA  Poorly differentiated CA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  7 CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a 14 x 16 x 7 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  and a 15 x 7 0cm skin ellipse with a nipple in the center  A firm mass is palpable directly below the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 7 x 6 x 6cm relatively well circumscribed tan to yellow nodular mass with focal cystic and soft regions  the largest cyst is 3cm in diameter and contains bloody fluid  The nodular mass grossly abuts against the posterior and inferior resection margin  Four representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  the closest margin  deep  is submitted in A  A representative section of a tan white  fibrous area that extends from the tumor to the inferior resection margin is submitted in cassette E  Similar fibrous tissue on the posterior deep resection margin is submitted in cassette F  which also contains another section of the fibrous tissue  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 0cm  submitted in cassettes G through L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 46 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma  REMOVED_CASE_ID   treated with radiation  R O recurrence                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  EXTENSIVE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN  NOTE  The tumor is approximately 50  in situ and 50  infiltrating  and is 1 5cm in greatest dimension  In situ carcinoma is present both within and away from the main tumor mass  Vascular invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 48                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 40     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 08 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of tissue with a needle and accompanying x ray  showing a nodular opacity with microcalcifications  The specimen contains a 1 5cm firm  gritty  tan gray nodule that grossly extends to the surgical margins  which are inked  Representative nodule tissue is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and kept frozen  The remainder of the breast is submitted in cassettes A through E  Each block has a portion of the nodule  Cassette F contains grossly normal tissue  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INTRADUCTAL AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST , Grossly_positive.
