sted cut surface  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  S  one lymph node bisected  T  one lymph node bisected  Gross Description by  CHRISTINE D AMATO Resident  ELENA BRACHTEL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  RE EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID    917  EXC PART C  BREAST RIGHT  INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE CAVITY SHAVED MARGIN  E PART D  BREAST RIGHT  SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE CAVITY SHAVED MARGIN  E , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 AUG 02 ACCESSIONED ON  02 AUG 02 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Calcifications on mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH EXTENSION INTO LOBULES  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Spanning at least 2 0cm  Grade  3  Calcifications  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ is focally present at the superoposterior and anterior margins of the specimen  NOTE  Definite invasive carcinoma is not identified  multiple levels examined  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  08 AUG 02 at 17 29                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  are 2 portions of yellow breast tissue  The larger portion measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm and is oriented with a long stitch lateral and short stitch superior  The smaller portion of breast tissue measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and is unoriented and has a localization needle in place  Larger fragment is inked black anteriorly  blue posteriorly and red for the superior rim  The larger fragment is serially sectioned revealing unremarkable tan white to yellow breast tissue  The larger fragment is entirely submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes A E  Small fragment has a localization needle  which is very superficially attached to the tissue  This fragment is entirely inked black and serially sectioned revealing tan white to yellow unremarkable breast tissue  This fragment is entirely submitted in cassettes F G  Resident  VINCENT KO  MD                                   