s with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a 21 x 15 x 4cm right modified radical mastectomy  Specimen with a 20 x 10cm overlying skin ellipse with a centrally located nipple and a 6 x 5 x 2 5cm axillary tail  The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm white yellow  focally cystic  firm mass of regular borders that is 0 1cm from the skin surface and 0 5cm from the deepest margin and 0 2cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  In the same mass  there is an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm of firm area that is 0 5cm from the deep margin  Representative section from the mass including the firm area are included in cassette A C and P S  Additional representative section from the mass are submitted in cassette D through I  A section away from the mass in cassette J  Lymph node dissected from the axillary tail are submitted in cassettes K through O  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    AXILLARY CONTENTS , Negative.
