Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 17 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO MARGIN  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 28 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   10   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 21     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 38 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 269 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of tissue  sectioned to reveal a firm  poorly defined  gray white tumor  measuring 3 0cm in greatest diameter  A portion is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  A piece is also taken for BRDU  as well as a piece embedded for hormonal analysis  Other representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through E  The tumor appears to be at the margin grossly  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LEFT BREAST LESION   INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST LESION , Grossly_positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AS MEASURED FROM A GLASS SLIDE  WITH CENTRAL HYALINIZING FIBROSIS AND NECROSIS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE WITHIN AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  LYMPH NODES   LEFT AXILLA  DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OUT OF 15 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY LEFT   TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 6 OUT OF 6 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  ADDITIONAL DEEP   RE EXCISION  BREAST TISSUE WITH STROMAL FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   CAUTERIZED BREAST TISSUE WITH INVOLUTIONAL CHANGE AND FOCAL MICROCALIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is seen  although several suspicious foci are identified  The examined margin of resection appears free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See Note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Labeled  wide excision  left breast  and received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  There is a short stitch and a long stitch designating the superior and the lateral margins resectively  The superior margin is inked in green and lateral in red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  ill defined nodule  present at 0 2cm from the closest inferior margin  A representative section of the nodule and inferior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  B to D are tumor with additional inferior margins  E to H are sections of superior margin  I and J are sections of the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue are multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension and disected from this fatty tissue which is submitted in cassettes K V  Cassettes M V contain half of each lymph node  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fatty tissue  Six lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm and disected from this fatty tissue  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes Q and R  Labeled  additional  superior and deep margin excision  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes S T and U  Labeled  additional  inferior to deep margin  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No lesion is identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes V and W  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECITON DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRAITING CARCINOMA  MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY  LEFT   CONTENTS PART C  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY  LEFT   TISSUE PART D  ADDITIONAL DEEP  RE EXCISION PART E  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   report_end  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  25   BOTH COMPONENTS FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Both invasive and in situ components of the tumor approach to within less than 0 1cm of several inked margins  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The main tumor mass grossly measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension  and includes both in situ and invasive tumor  Foci of in situ carcinoma are also present well apart from the main tumor mass  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  more invasive areas were present on additional sections than on the section frozen for intraoperative evaluation  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fairly well circumscribed 1 0cm rubbery  pink tan to white focus abutting several inked margins  representative section of lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A E  The frozen is submitted in cassette F  No BRDU or estrogen and progesterone receptors are sent  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  RULE OUT INVASION  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Focally_close.
