oval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 08 49     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     Note  Microscopic foci of DCIS are present in 13 of 15 slides sampled  Added by  JOSEPH T  RABBAN  M D   M P H  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm specimen of fibrofatty tissue with 2 needle localization wires running through it and a long stitch demarcating the medial surface and a short stitch demarcating the inferior surface as per the surgeon s note on the requisition form  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  Sectioning through the specimen reveals a tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  Abutting the lateral edge of the specimen  there is a 0 5cm in diameter hemorrhagic area which also abuts the anterior and inferior margins  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic area which abuts the inferior and posterior margins and is 1 2cm from the anterior surgical margin and 3 3cm from the superior margin and 0 4cm from the lateral margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm nodular cavity containing a 0 3cm in diameter nodule 0 5cm from the medial margin of the specimen  This cavity is 1 5cm from the anterior surgical margin  1 0cm from the posterior surgical margin  1 3cm from the inferior surgical margin and 2 0cm from the superior surgical margin  The specimen is entirely submitted serially from lateral to medial in cassettes A O with the first lateral most hemorrhagic area in cassette A  the more medial hemorrhagic area in cassette E and the nodular area in the more medial region of the specimen in cassettes J N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow nodular soft tissue which is trisected and submitted in cassettes P R  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   BIOPSY , Negative.
