gned on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 04   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 55 28AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  107  to chromosome 17 signals  218  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 06   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 44 38PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Breast  Left   Excision PART C  Breast  Left   Biopsy PART D  Breast  Left  Medial Margin   Excision PART E  Breast  Left  Superior Margin   Excision PART F  Breast  Left  Posterior Margin   Excision PART G  Breast  Left  Inferior Margin   Excision  report_end  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 06 CLINICAL DATA  Previous excision outside with broadly positive margins  need ER PR stains  if residual tumor                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH LOBULAR FEATURES  GRADE 2  EXTENDING TO DEEP FASCIA  JUST SUPERFICIAL TO SKELETAL MUSCLE   INVOLVING A SUPERIOR MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND A MEDIAL MARGIN FOCALLY  SEE NOTE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Residual tumor is multifocal and present in 5 of 7 sections  The greatest tumor dimension  measured from slide B  is 1 6cm  No lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Immunostains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed on section B  and the results reported in an addendum  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE  NEW  MARGIN  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SMALL FIBROADENOMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL TUMOR  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   REGIONAL NODE DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four parts  Labeled  left breast lump  is breast tissue with a small skin ellipse and a biopsy cavity  After the margins are inked black  one slice near the medial aspect  not the actual margin  is frozen as frozen section  1  now submitted as A  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm fragment of breast has attached black sutures designated as  short suture superior  long suture lateral   The superior aspect is inked green  over black ink   The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm tan white  ill defined stellate mass  which grossly extends to the superior  superficial  deep and medial margins  A representative section of the mass where it abuts the superior superficial and deep margins is submitted in B  The most medial margin is taken en face  breadloafed and submitted entirely in C  Two other representative sections of tumor are submitted in D and E  Two other sections of tissue not associated with the mass are submitted in F and G  Labeled  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm aggregate of fat containing lymph nodes from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted and submitted in cassettes H through K  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number only  but designated on the accessioning sheet as  left breast additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of breast with an attached black suture designated by the surgeon as  Margin furthest away from biopsy cavity   The specimen is inked entirely in black  The sutured aspect of this specimen is over inked in green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable tissue and submitted entirely in cassetts L through N  Labeled  left breast lump  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm fragment of breast and an attached black suture designated by the surgeon as  Stitch marks edge furthest from tumor   The entire specimen is inked black  The aspect with the suture is over inked in green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue and submitted entirely in O through U  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION  1  BREAST  LEFT MARGIN   SUSPICIOUS FOR RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  IN AREA OF CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FIBROSIS  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART D  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION   report_end  , Grossly_close_(multifocal/_broad_front).
