Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  OMReceived fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm breast with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan pink skin ellipse  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm unremarkable nipple and areola  No previous incision site on the skin is noted  There is an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary fat pad  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan white  finely granular mass with ill defined borders  This mass comes to within 1 4cm of the posterior  closest  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is approximately 80  fatty and 20  fibrous tissue  The fibrous tissue is predominantly dense granular and cystic  Within the axillary fat pad multiple lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Tumor to posterior margin C D  Tumor E F  Representative of fibrous tissue G J  Whole lymph nodes K  One lymph node bisected Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node level 1   are two fatty lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  which are bisected and entirely submitted as FX  1 and FX  2  now as L and M respectively  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node level 2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fatty lymph node  which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX  3 and FX  4  now as N and O  respectively  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX 1 2  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL LEVEL ONE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FXDX 3 4  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL LEVEL TWO   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SONER ALTIOK  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Janey Sue Pratt  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LEVEL I  PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LEVEL II  , Grossly_close_(multifocal/_broad_front).
