g of the invasive and in situ components may not be entirely accurate  There is striking fibrosis within the tumor which is likely secondary to chemotherapy effect  The lymph nodes show marked therapy related fibrosis as well  The metastatic tumor within the lymph nodes consists of aggregates of tumor   0 2cm  and single cells scattered throughout the fibrotic stroma  Cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stains help confirm the presence of tumor cells within the more fibrotic lymph nodes  No definite extracapsular extension is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN FOUR OUT OF FOUR LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lymph nodes show significant fibrosis  consistent with chemotherapy effect  Cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stains confirm the presence of scattered tumor cells within the more fibrotic lymph nodes  There is tumor present within extranodal lymphatic vessels  but no definite extracapsular extension is identified  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right modified radical mastectomy  is a an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm axillary tail  The specimen is surfaced by an REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan pink areola  The areola comes to 1 8cm of the superior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unremarkable tan pink nipple which comes to 2 2cm of the closest inferior margin  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a fairly well defined  largely centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm indurated tan pink mass with several contiguous peripheral nodules predominantly along the inferior and medial aspects of the primary mass  N B  the overall measurement of the mass includes these contiguous nodules    The mass comes to 0 7cm of the posterior  and 1 4cm of the anterior margin  The remaining mammary tissue is unremarkable  Sectioning of the attached axillary tail reveals multiple tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass from lateral to medial  with closest approach to deep margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and closest approach to anterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative peripheral nodular areas along the inferior and medial aspects of the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Finely nodular fibrous area  lateral aspect of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue medial to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph nodes  in toto    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  bisected   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   additional tissue right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of lymph node bearing tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progeste